WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
What the first half of the lecture builds.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:14.040
micrograd is a tiny autograd engine: a library that records the arithmetic you do on numbers and can then compute the derivative of the final result with respect to every input.

3
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:23.259
The repository’s README describes it as roughly 100 lines for the engine plus 50 for a small neural network library on top.

4
00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:27.763
It works on scalars only, which makes it slow and perfectly transparent.

5
00:00:28.043 --> 00:00:36.811
The first 87 minutes of the video, which this lesson covers, go from “what is a derivative” to a working backward() on arbitrary expressions.

6
00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:43.789
The second half (next lesson) builds neurons, a multilayer perceptron, a loss, and a training loop on top of it.
